codemirror.js is one ES module built from build/entry.js with esbuild 0.25.11 against the
exact versions in build/package.json and build/package-lock.json:

    cd build && npm ci && npx esbuild entry.js --bundle --format=esm --minify \
        --legal-comments=none --target=es2022 --outfile=../codemirror.js

sha256 of codemirror.js: afc0c5282b0b14a1093ed99e9144f183c2d971b22970548ae1797e4cbaf43478

It exports createEditor(parent, {text, name, readOnly, onChange, onSave}), createDiff(parent,
{left, right, name}) and languageFor(name). Its colours are the page's CSS variables. The Web
server serves only codemirror.js from this folder (STATIC_FILES in app.py); the editor loads it
on first use.
